# oracle: pair_style hybrid/overlay (lj/cut 2.5 and coul/cut 3.0, pair_modify shift yes) on a charged 2-type fcc LJ box of 108 atoms: 5 steps, write_restart, clear, read_restart (the sub-style list and settings come back, the coefficients do not: pair_coeff is given again), 5 more steps; per-atom compare
# engine vs native fixture: measured below
# native: installed lmp (b332f28)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      charge
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
region          half block INF 1.5 INF INF INF INF
set             region half type 2
set             type 1 charge 0.0
set             type 2 charge -1.0
mass            * 1.0
velocity        all create 1.2 4321 loop geom
pair_style      hybrid/overlay lj/cut 2.5 coul/cut 3.0
pair_coeff      1 1 lj/cut 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 lj/cut 1.0 0.9
pair_coeff      * * coul/cut
pair_modify     shift yes
timestep        0.002
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl ecoul press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             5
write_restart   w177px_hybrid.restart
clear
read_restart    w177px_hybrid.restart
pair_coeff      1 1 lj/cut 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 lj/cut 1.0 0.9
pair_coeff      * * coul/cut
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe evdwl ecoul press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             5
